claim.claim-text:
monitoring, by a network monitor (320), network conditions of a communications link (340, 350) utilized to transmit to a remote display (360) video image data of a surgical procedure, the video image data being captured by an endoscopic image capture device (305) located at a remote surgical site of the surgical procedure;
automatically determining, by the network monitor (320), that a change in the network conditions that will affect transmission of the video image data to the remote display (360) is expected to occur, the determining occurring before the change in the network conditions occurs;
adjusting an encoding configuration of a video encoder (310) in response to determining that the change in network conditions is expected to occur;
encoding the video image data of the surgical procedure captured after the change of the network conditions, the encoding using the video encoder (310) having the adjusted encoding configuration; and
outputting the encoded video image data for transmission to the remote display (360).

an endoscopic image capture device (305) for capturing image data of a surgical site during a surgical procedure;
an input device (355) for receiving a control command input, the input device (355) being operably coupled to control at least one of the endoscopic image capture device (305) and a surgical instrument (125) of the surgical system;
a network monitor (320) for determining network conditions of a communications link (340, 350) utilized to transmit video of the image data to a remote display (360) during the surgical procedure, the network monitor (320) configured to determine that a change in the network conditions that will affect transmission of the image data to the remote display (360) is expected to occur, the determining occurring before the change in the network conditions occurs; and
a video processor (325) for generating video encoding configuration data to encode the video of the image data, the video processor (325) configured to:
output adjusted video encoding configuration data based on an input received from the network monitor (320) indicating that the change in network conditions is expected to occur.

receive from the video processor (325) the video encoding configuration data;
receive from the endoscopic image capture device (305) the image data;
encode the video of the image data based on the received video encoding configuration data; and
output the encoded video of the image data for transmission to the remote display (360).

a state monitor (315) configured to determine that a change of state of the surgical system is expected to occur and that the change of state is anticipated to have an effect on image content of the image data;
wherein the adjusted video encoding configuration data comprises an intra-frames, i-frames, rate parameter and a predictive inter-frames, p-frames, rate parameter; and
the video processor (325) is configured to adjust the i-frames rate parameter and the p-frames rate parameter based on the input received from the network monitor (320) indicating that the change in network conditions is expected to occur and based on an input from the state monitor (315) indicating the anticipated effect of the change of state of the surgical system.

a state monitor (315) configured to determine that a change of state of the surgical system is expected to occur and that the change of state is anticipated to have an effect on image content of the image data;
wherein the adjusted video encoding configuration data comprises an image encoding resolution and/or an image encoding bit rate or frame rate; and
the video processor (325) is configured to adjust the encoding resolution and/or an image encoding bit rate or frame rate parameters based on the input received from the network monitor (320) indicating that the change in network conditions is expected to occur and based on an input from the state monitor (315) indicating the anticipated effect of the change of state of the surgical system.
